3	// Step 7c of DEVDESK-580 (PR2), the command half of `nexus-bench record`: three
4	// flags and what --state does. The tests of record_cmd_test.go (no flag, no
5	// cluster) stay as they are; the rig is theirs (newRecordRig).
6	//
7	//   - --state nominal|upstream-cut. Without it nothing changes: the command
8	//     opens no runner, runs no preflight and reads no upstream (the events stay
9	//     [newStore record]), and RecordOptions.State is the zero value. With it the
10	//     command, after the descriptor, the deny list and the secrets and BEFORE the
11	//     library runs, builds the runner, runs the preflight OpRecord (a read of the
12	//     Deployment and the pods), reads the upstream (ReadUpstream, read only) and
13	//     compares: nominal wants UpstreamReady, upstream-cut wants UpstreamCut, any
14	//     other state refuses, with exit 1, a message that names the declared state,
15	//     and record never called, so not a single request is sent. nominal maps to
16	//     nexusbench.StateNominal (the zero value), upstream-cut to
17	//     nexusbench.StateUpstreamCut. Nothing else of the cluster is touched.
18	//   - --allow-cache-effects sets RecordOptions.AllowCacheEffects, with no cluster
19	//     access of its own.
20	//   - --request-timeout sets RecordOptions.RequestTimeout; the default is 15s
21	//     (the option may carry 0 or 15s, both mean 15 s), shown in the help.
22	//   - The three flags are record's: the other subcommands refuse them (usage
23	//     error). An unknown --state or an unparsable duration is a usage error too
24	//     (exit 2, before any dependency); a negative duration is refused, before
25	//     record.
26	//   - When the report lists fixtures sent with a cache effect, the output names them
27	//     and asks for a reset; a report without any says nothing of a reset.
28	
29	import (
30		"bytes"
31		"errors"
32		"os"
33		"slices"
34		"strings"
35		"testing"
36		"time"
37	
38		"github.com/anthnel/devdesk/internal/nexusbench"
39	)
